#!/bin/bash
# Crypto Screener V2 loop — self-paced, read roadmap and execute first unchecked task
# Run: claude "/loop $(tail -1 CRYPTO_LOOP_V2.sh)"
# Or paste the last line into claude with /loop

Read docs/CRYPTO_SCREENER_V2_ROADMAP.md and follow its hard rules exactly. Do only the first unchecked [ ] task. Hard rules recap: NO new serverless files under apps/market-ui/api — all server data via ?view= branches (spot/technicals/derivatives/meta) in api/crypto/markets.ts; fns stay pinned "regions":["fra1"] in vercel.json (Binance 451-blocks US Vercel IPs — never remove); keyless APIs only (Binance spot+fapi futures/data, DeFiLlama, CoinGecko free) and curl-verify each NEW endpoint returns real data BEFORE coding against it; no new npm deps — all indicator math hand-rolled on the SAME klines already fetched (never a second klines call per symbol); llama /protocols is multi-MB so keep only a {symbol→tvl} map w/ 1h cache, CG category calls ≤8 w/ 1h cache; payloads additive only — v1 fields and coingecko→coinlore→okx chain untouched; every new ColKey gets exactly one th and one td (parity), colCount stays 4+toggled; UI uses project design tokens matching existing Markets.tsx popovers. Verify per task: market-ui typecheck 0 + vercel --prod + prod curl with REAL numbers pasted into the Progress log. Flip the task to [x], append one Progress-log line with real numbers, commit on roadmap/world-class (git commit -F file if the message has quotes — rtk mangles them). PERSISTENCE: never end the loop because of a usage/rate limit, 429, or overloaded error — on any such error stop consuming tokens, ScheduleWakeup at 3600s with this exact /loop prompt, and on wake re-read the ledger and resume the same task from its last verified step (ledger + Progress log are recovery state; log partial progress BEFORE long/risky operations); chain hourly wakeups as needed. Only stop for: no [ ] remaining, or a task blocked on something only the user can provide — then say exactly what's needed and still ScheduleWakeup (3600s) so the loop resumes if supplied.
